ant  to make money self i want to see zorro  or sanji just calmly being like no way  luffy's dead but we obviously don't get  that here and zoro is probably not  getting up anytime soon kaido then shows  why he's clearly not joyboy joyboy is  associated with liberation and kaido  says this country is a weapons factory  to him he doesn't care if they're woman  or children everyone is his slave so  yeah kaido is no hero no surprise there  there was a rebellion and now he's going  to make sure his enemies work until they  drop dead that's how they'll live the  rest of their miserable lives according  to him there's a great terrifying panel  of him saying you chose to oppose me  facing my wrath now should come as no  surprise and although he's morally wrong  to do it it's realistic and everyone  should have expected as much or worse if  kaido won a samurai is panicking saying  no please spare my wife and child but it  ain't happening as kaido says that is  what it means to lose in war you gambled  with your rights and dreams he then says  this doesn't end until they bring him  momo in the meantime weak extra beast  pirates go to finish off the weekend kid  in law since they are high off of  kaido's victory our two supernova look  like they can't even move and their men  step in to protect them one dude also  says kaido is tougher than a fortress  which is a cool line and i have to agree  with that kaido just might be the  physically toughest dude i can think of  panic is the general state of things as  people run around looking for a way out  as the flames spread kid in law get up  kid says i'm fighting surrendering or  letting him kill us are both out of the  question and you gotta love it i've been  saying for a long time i love kid's  character and this attitude in the face  of another yonko coming after he beat  the first is just so respectable and  commendable law doesn't sound quite as  determined and he's more upset with  luffy for not pulling off his side of  the deal but we can imagine he'll follow  kid's example as best as he can when he  doesn't have a choice then we have momo  and yamato yamato wants momo to fight  kaido and it would be interesting to see  momo's new power in combat if only until  luffy interrupts the fight momo is as  usual scared and not wanting to fight  against kaido because he feels like  he'll just lose especially if even luffy  lost yamato tells him he can fight until  his last breath isn't that the way of  the samurai and again we have the way of  the samurai honorable death discussion  coming about and whereas it is a very  cool code no doubt the arc has made us  question the value of an honorable death  there may be times when it's the only  way but by this point oda has definitely  encouraged us to look for alternative  routes to victory after all odin's death  was epic and very honorable but it would  still be more valuable if he found a way  to survive and actually beat kaido if  everyone strong keeps dying honorable  deaths there will soon be nobody to stop  kaido and protect wano i do respect  yamato though as the daughter of odin  she's ready to fight to the end with  momo she says if not us who everyone is  at their limit and even kaido must be  feeling it now which yeah i wonder how  much he is feeling it because he is good  at not letting anybody notice that he is  feeling anything momo thinks with luffy  gone the only option is to yield and not  throw away more lives yamato who  remember is associated with a guardian  deity of wano through her fruit wants to  defend wano by fighting she refuses to  accept the people of wano being slaves  until the day they die not thinking that  that's any better than death she says  suffering won't save anyone and momo is  panicked not sure what to do she says  all the daimyo that allowed rochi to  have his way went to their graves full  of regret everything wano endured for  the past 20 years was for the sake of  this battle and there's something 